Z||000000||LePetiteGT||09-15-1999||11:12 PM||||Hi Guys,<BR>I just wanted you to know that today I bought a "new" 86 Fiero GT!! I`m real proud of myself.... I`ve wanted one for myself since <BR>I saw my boyfriend`s Black GT. He hasn`t had<BR>his very long so he`s not too knowledgable in<BR>this area so I come to you folks for some advice: This car is in pretty good shape it just needs a Woman`s touch and some TLC but I`m not sure what I should do first. It needs<BR>a paint job since the origional red paint is fading, the headlights are in the up position and the switch just turns the lights on and off, the hood won`t open so I can see what`s wrong,the rear bumper is starting to hang separating from the rear taillights and the factory radio doesn`t work! I need some suggestions from you guys especially Theogre<BR>as to where I go from here! Thanks!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||batboy||09-15-1999||11:58 PM||||I hate it when Ogre gets all the Fiero ladies swooning over him. Just kidding. How come the Fiero ladies always have hubbies or boyfriends? *sigh* Not kidding about that one. The headlight problem could be bad motors, relays, or gears. Toss the radio and get a nice CD player. You might want to check the fuse first though. Sometimes people will remove their fancy stereo before selling the car and stick the old radio back in without hooking it back up. The hood not opening might be a broken release cable or if the car got hit in the nose, it could be that the safety lugs have been engaged. Pray it's not the second possibility. There is actually a second cable to release the hood if the first one is broken. Look closely at the hood release lever, right next to it is the spare cable, slip it out of the holder and pull on it (carefully use pliers if need be). Hope that helps you get started.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_MOM||09-16-1999||01:13 AM||||Hey Girl!  Welcome to the Fiero Forum.  I'm am extremely excited to have another gal on the forum.  I guess you better let your other half know, he'd better be careful of what he wishes for!  I can imagine the questions you must have about where to start, but don't worry, before you know it, you will be a true Fiero know it all.  I have been thinking alot lately about purchasing a Fiero for myself so that I don't have to share with my husband, DXR_DAD, but he does let me drive his and I've starting to prefer that little (only mid-engine, 2 seater, American made sports car ever made). Enjoy and look forward to hearing from you on the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||09-16-1999||03:16 AM||||<BR>Hey batboy, you sly dog. You just came back from a trip to the Minnesota State Fair and  Mystic Lakes Casino with your "lady friend", and now you're whining about all the Fiero ladies being taken? You're not slowing down in your old age, are you? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ogre may attract all the ladies, but as soon as he fixes their car, they're gone. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Of course, I'm neither attracting nor travelling with any ladies lately, so I'll just go off and sulk now... <P>Actually, I learned something from batboy's post. I had NO idea what that silver cable was under my dash. Now I do.<P>Oh, by the way, welcome to the forum LePetiteGT.<P> ||||reg||12
